# Go conventions

- **File layout** (`var` → `const` → type units → package func), constants, exported godoc, readability: follow [go-structure.mdc](go-structure.mdc); line width 150, nesting ≤2, readability-first, function block spacing — see §8–§11; required when generating or refactoring Go code
- Indent with **tabs**; run `make fmt` (or `go fmt ./...`) on touched packages
- Tests: `*_test.go` beside implementation; keep `make test` green
- `internal/` packages are module-private — app code belongs in `internal/ssh` (package `aissh`), not duplicated in `cmd/`
- Prefer standard library; add dependencies only when needed
- Error handling: return errors from `Run` and callers; avoid silent `catch` patterns

```go
// cmd/aissh — keep thin
func main() {
    if err := ait.Run(os.Args[1:]); err != nil {
        os.Exit(1)
    }
}
```
